        'details.metaballs.title': 'Metaballs',
        'details.metaballs.start_scene': 'Start metaballs scene',
        'details.metaballs.preview_alt': 'Screenshot of the metaballs scene',
        'details.metaballs.text_1': 'The lava is made of metaballs: every ball spreads a field that fades with distance. The visible surface lies wherever the summed fields cross a threshold. Neighbouring balls therefore don’t just overlap – they melt into one soft, continuous body, which is exactly how viscous lava appears to behave.',
        'details.metaballs.scroll_hint': 'About metaballs',
        'details.metaballs.description.field_heading': 'The potential of a metaball',
        'details.metaballs.description.field_text_1': 'Every ball i with its centre cᵢ assigns a value, its potential, to every point p in space. It depends only on the distance rᵢ between p and the centre:',
        'details.metaballs.description.field_text_2': 'The falloff function φᵢ gets smaller as the distance grows: close to the centre the potential is large, further away it is small. Its exact shape decides how softly the balls blend into one another. Common choices are, for example:',
        'details.metaballs.description.falloff_reciprocal': 'reciprocal',
